## Original Content
Le chef du gouvernement malien, Abdoulaye Maïga, s'est rendu en Algérie ce lundi pour une visite de travail. Il a été reçu par le président Abdelmadjid Tebboune, dans un contexte de rapprochement après plusieurs années de tensions entre les deux pays. Correspondance de Serge Daniel.

## Summary
Abdoulaye Maïga, Mali's government chief, visited Algeria on Monday to improve bilateral relations after years of tensions. He was received by Algerian President Abdelmadjid Tebboune in a move to foster a rapprochement between the two nations.

## Key Points
- Mali's government chief Abdoulaye Maïga traveled to Algeria for a work visit
- The visit aimed to relaunch relations after several years of tensions between Mali and Algeria
- Algerian President Abdelmadjid Tebboune hosted Maïga during the visit
- The meeting signifies a diplomatic effort to mend ties between the two countries


